"""Wiring integration tests for the three guard layers (AIT-50).

These tests exist because `guardrails/guards.py` previously passed a full
behavioural suite while being called by nothing on any graph path. Testing the
guard functions in isolation proves they WORK; only these tests prove they RUN.
Each docstring names the exact edit that makes the test fail — an assertion
that survives deleting the wiring is not a wiring test.

The TypeScript twin is `tests/guards-wiring.test.ts`; the layers are the same
three, and the seams differ only because that runtime streams.
"""

